        "si_used": true,
        "procedure": "Ni(AcO)2·4H2O (186.6 mg, 0.75 mmol), aqueous Er(ClO4)3 (1.25 mL, 1.25 mmol; prepared as a 1 M solution by digesting Er2O3 in concentrated perchloric acid), and (R)-H3L (60 mg, 0.25 mmol; H3L = (2-hydroxy-3-methoxybenzyl)serine, made by the literature method) were added to 10 mL deionized water. The solution was heated to about 60 °C, the pH was adjusted to about 6.2 with freshly prepared 0.5 M aqueous NaOH, and the mixture was refluxed for 1 h and filtered. Evaporation of the filtrate under ambient conditions gave light-blue rhombic crystals after one week.",
