        "summary": "Oriented single-crystal χMT is 63.49 cm3 K mol−1 at room temperature and falls to 34.37 cm3 K mol−1 at 2.0 K; magnetization saturates near 37 μB at 2.0 K, with low Er(III) anisotropy. Magneto-chiral dichroism is strong for the magnetic-dipole-allowed Er(III) 4I13/2 ← 4I15/2 transition, with gMChD = 0.24(1) T−1 at 1516.2 nm (4.0 K, 1.0 T), much larger than the other f–f and Ni(II) d–d transitions; the signal remains detectable at room temperature (gMChD = 0.054(1) T−1 at 1530 nm) and tracks the magnetization.",
